<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Dahomey</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dahomey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Dahomey was a West African kingdom centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abomey">Abomey</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, known for its centralised monarchy and its role in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. In the eighteenth century it was forced to pay tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> after repeated Oyo cavalry invasions. It later freed itself from Oyo's overlordship and was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the 1890s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Dahomey" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_banner_of_B%C3%A9hanzin_of_Dahomey.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
